1
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten up and try stepping away.

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,420
Like someone calling out
after the rain has stopped.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,280
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:42,340
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,640
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,100
the politicians with their pompous faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Go ahead and turn that corner.

11
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:19,880
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,780
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,960
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,360
Pokero in the anime!

16
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:47,000
Hijack! Hijack!

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,560
My Robo-Deka Bancho

18
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:52,120
Senpai,
your manga is still being serialized?

19
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,460
Who on earth reads this stuff?

20
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,027
Well, you two couldn't possibly

21
00:01:56,077 --> 00:01:59,460
understand how brilliant my manga is.

22
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:04,080
Boss Ryotsu, big trouble!

23
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:08,360
What? They've decided
on a TV anime adaptation?

24
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:11,960
Yes. Mr. Ryu Senshi from
Weekly Sapphire said so.

25
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:16,740
Wow! Yes! The day has finally come!

26
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:21,300
Is getting an anime adaptation
really such a big deal?

27
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,540
Of course it is!

28
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:26,960
A 10% viewer rating means
about 10 million people,

29
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:30,600
and at 20%,
that's 20 million people watching.

30
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,160
Recognition goes up by an enormous amount.

31
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:38,040
So naturally,
the original tankōbon will sell, sell, sell!

32
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:42,300
Tie-in merchandise will keep coming out,
and that will sell like crazy too.

33
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:45,960
The mangaka who created the
original work will soar in fame,

34
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:48,680
and be in constant demand for
TV appearances and lectures.

35
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:53,640
With the royalties and appearance fees from all of that,
you can rake in a huge fortune!

36
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:56,140
Hello.

37
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,020
Nana-chan.

38
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:01,660
I just heard from Honda-san.
Congratulations, Nana-chan!

39
00:03:01,660 --> 00:03:02,840
Congratulations!

40
00:03:02,840 --> 00:03:04,420
Yes, thank you very much.

41
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,640
Hey, what exactly is there to celebrate?

42
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:10,080
Well, it's getting an
anime adaptation, right?

43
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:11,640
Nana-chan's Menate...

44
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:14,660
Isn't it my Robo-Teka Banchō?

45
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:18,860
Come on, senpai,
I never said anything like that.

46
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,257
The one getting the anime adaptation is

47
00:03:20,307 --> 00:03:23,442
the one Nana-chan writes
under the pen name Ai no Miko,

48
00:03:23,492 --> 00:03:24,940
this Menate, you know.

49
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,720
No way!

50
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:28,950
Makoto-kun, Ai-chan.

51
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,580
Makoto-kun, Ai-chan. Makoto-kun,

52
00:03:31,630 --> 00:03:33,320
Ai-chan. Makoto-kun,

53
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:35,980
Ai-chan. Makoto-kun, Ai-chan.

54
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:41,300
It's just the same thing over and over! I have no
idea what's supposed to be interesting about it!

55
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:43,480
Senpai, that's rude to Nana-chan!

56
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:44,580
That's right!

57
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:45,220
That's cruel.

58
00:03:45,220 --> 00:03:47,620
Something that isn't interesting
just isn't interesting.

59
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:50,300
I can't understand the person who would
make something like this into an anime.

60
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:54,120
If they're making an anime, it should
be Robo Deka Banchou first, obviously!

61
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,500
What are you talking about?

62
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:59,100
Minuet is a million times more
interesting than Ryo-chan's manga.

63
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,540
What? What's so
interesting about this manga?

64
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,260
For one thing,
the art is prettier than Ryo-chan's.

65
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:10,000
Besides,
the story developments are interesting too.

66
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,280
Above all, the subtle psychological
portrayal of the girls is great, isn't it?

67
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:20,839
Who needs that anymore! Come on! What
a work needs to be adapted into anime is

68
00:04:20,889 --> 00:04:24,800
impact and power,
and above all, man's dream!

69
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:28,496
Weekly Sapphire is a
magazine that girls read.

70
00:04:28,546 --> 00:04:30,620
Man's dreams aren't needed at all.

71
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:34,540
Honestly, it's strange that your manga is
being serialized in the first place, isn't it?

72
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:39,700
I heard they're only keeping it going because
they figure you'd complain if they cancelled it.

73
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:42,140
Shut up! What do amateurs know?

74
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:44,440
Most readers are amateurs.

75
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:47,160
My manga is a masterpiece that
will be remembered for generations!

76
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:50,940
It's not like some limp,
wishy-washy manga like Menet!

77
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:52,485
My manga is...

78
00:04:52,535 --> 00:04:55,760
So that's how men see it.

79
00:04:55,900 --> 00:04:59,580
N-no, that's not true.
Even I, a man, find it really interesting.

80
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:04,148
Nana-chan, this is a wish that manga artists
who will never get adapted into anime have,

81
00:05:04,198 --> 00:05:05,120
so don't mind it.

82
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:07,040
That's right, Nana-chan.

83
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:07,860
I see.

84
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:11,420
Oh no! I have to get going!

85
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,600
Is it already that late?

86
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:14,620
What, are you going somewhere?

87
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,380
It's for a press coverage
of the dubbing session.

88
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:18,980
The voice recording for the first episode
of the Ai no Miko anime

89
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:20,340
is happening today.

90
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:23,400
I've arranged to observe
it as a special guest,

91
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:25,140
so take me with you too!

92
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:27,020
As a fellow writer,

93
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:28,480
I have a duty to see

94
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,060
what kind of anime it'll become.

95
00:05:30,060 --> 00:05:33,440
Ai no Miko is the flagship title of Weekly Sapphire,
after all.

96
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:35,780
You were tearing it apart
just a moment ago, though!

97
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:41,660
So this is the recording studio.

98
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:44,000
Who are these people?

99
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:46,140
Good morning.

100
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:48,180
Morning.

101
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:51,140
Those are fans of the voice actress.

102
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,620
Having stalkers too, she's really popular.

103
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:57,860
Is Ryu-senshu from Weekly Sapphire here?

104
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:58,900
Hey, Miko.

105
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,960
Everyone, this is Ai no Miko-sensei,
the original creator of Minuet.

106
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:04,680
Good morning.

107
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,520
Good morning.

108
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:07,660
Come on, Miko, this way.

109
00:06:07,660 --> 00:06:08,500
Excuse me.

110
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,060
Pardon the intrusion.

111
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,820
Yo, Ryu-senshi! I came to see you!

112
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:14,460
Hey, Ryo-san!

113
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:17,180
Why are you even here?

114
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:20,591
Hey, if Minuet is getting an anime,

115
00:06:20,641 --> 00:06:24,940
that means my Robo Deka Banchō
is getting one too, right?

116
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:28,220
Of course not. Use your common sense.

117
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:30,180
If not, go pitch it yourself!

118
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,700
Don't be unreasonable.

119
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:34,200
Why don't you just give up already.

120
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,060
Makato-kun!

121
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:37,280
W-who's that voice?

122
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:39,400
Mika, wait a moment.

123
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:44,060
Isn't that Sashi Hanazono,
the popular voice actress?

124
00:06:44,060 --> 00:06:48,740
Yes, I had her in mind too,
so I voted for her at the audition.

125
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:52,680
She's perfect for Ai's voice.
I'm really moved.

126
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:56,160
Honda, don't tell me
you're an anime nerd too!

127
00:06:56,160 --> 00:07:01,420
The first half of the after-recording is done,
so let's head inside.

128
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,840
Come on,
let's take a photo with the voice actors.

129
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:04,720
Yes.

130
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:09,980
We're here from Weekly Sapphire for an interview.
Nice to meet you all.

131
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:11,720
Nice to meet you.

132
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,080
This is Ms. Hanazono, who plays Ai,
and Mr. Kanzaki, who plays Makoto.

133
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:18,280
Nice to meet you, I'm Ai no Miko.

134
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,540
I'm Tenpei Kanzaki.

135
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:22,720
And there's Emi Kihara and Tsuyoshi Kobori.

136
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:25,440
Umeko Tange and Shigeru Sasa. I'm moved.

137
00:07:26,540 --> 00:07:29,180
So you finally came out, Honda.

138
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:32,100
Miko, the director just told me something.

139
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:34,720
He asked whether I'd like to
try reading a girl's lines.

140
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,660
Because your voice is really distinctive.

141
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:39,900
When I pitched that idea
in the gravure section...

142
00:07:41,520 --> 00:07:43,160
Are you really sure about this?

143
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:44,240
Yes, please!

144
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:48,280
I'm so happy!
I've always admired voice actors.

145
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:51,520
No way, Nana-chan is joining too?

146
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:54,480
She already has an anime voice,
so she's perfect just as she is.

147
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:58,160
Voice work for DVDs and videos?
What a sweet job!

148
00:07:58,160 --> 00:08:00,960
You get excited about everything, don't you?

149
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:07,680
Makoto-kun

150
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:08,860
Ai-chan

151
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,500
Makoto-kun

152
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:11,720
Ai-chan

153
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:13,340
Nakata-kun

154
00:08:13,340 --> 00:08:14,140
Ai-chan

155
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:17,420
The two of them were swayed
by the premonition of love.

156
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,280
Wonderful.

157
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:30,240
It's truly a wonderful work.

158
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,400
Thank you, director.

159
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,640
I'm counting on you going forward.

160
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:35,620
Thanks.

161
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:38,980
Honestly,
that editor-in-chief is so over the top.

162
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,320
What's wrong, Honda?

163
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:44,820
It was really great.

164
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:48,080
And it captures the original's
atmosphere perfectly.

165
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:51,320
This is the greatest shōjo anime ever,
seriously.

166
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:52,360
I see.

167
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:53,660
It's amazing.

168
00:08:53,660 --> 00:08:57,480
I never imagined my manga
would become such a lovely anime.

169
00:08:57,480 --> 00:09:00,180
With this, I can set off for
Europe with peace of mind, Miko.

170
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:00,940
Yay!

171
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:01,740
Europe.

172
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:05,120
The second part of Minuet is set in Europe,
you know.

173
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,160
That's why I'm going on a research trip.

174
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:13,400
I'm thinking of taking my time touring
the countries of Europe with everyone.

175
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:20,900
Well then,
shall we get ready to leave right away?

176
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:21,340
Yes.

177
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:25,360
Those guys, weren't they...

178
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,800
Do you know them?

179
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:31,680
Yeah, that's the old man from Tateishi
Toys who made my life-size figure.

180
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:35,860
Ryotsu-san.

181
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:37,900
Why the gloomy face?

182
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,460
It hasn't come out.

183
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:41,380
What hasn't?

184
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,960
Our toys haven't come out, you know.

185
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,320
Not a single place.

186
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:50,900
Your company is also a sponsor of this show,
you know.

187
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:53,940
So they made character merchandise

188
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:56,960
and asked to have it
featured during the show,

189
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:59,800
but it seems they were completely ignored.

190
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,920
So what kind of toy did they make?

191
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:03,760
This one, here.

192
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,700
It's the Love Transformation Tambourine Set.

193
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:09,615
Hey, look, Minuet is a pure love story,

194
00:10:09,665 --> 00:10:13,025
and the heroine, Kisaragi Ai,
is an ordinary high school girl!

195
00:10:13,075 --> 00:10:15,300
Why would she need to transform?

196
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:18,660
Actually, we've even come up
with a transformation pose, sir.

197
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:19,280
Yes.

198
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:25,042
Tō, paranni parenra, baterenren,

199
00:10:25,092 --> 00:10:28,060
kurukuru miracle, lovely change.

200
00:10:28,340 --> 00:10:32,320
We were hoping you'd use it for the heroine,
Kisaragi Ai.

201
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:33,760
As if we could use that.

202
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:37,400
But if it doesn't appear in the show,
there's no promotional effect.

203
00:10:37,400 --> 00:10:40,560
Ryo-san,
please somehow get it into the anime.

204
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:43,360
Could you persuade the staff for us?

205
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,320
Don't be unreasonable.

206
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:48,260
If you manage it,
we'll pay you a suitable reward.

207
00:10:49,180 --> 00:10:50,280
A reward

208
00:10:50,280 --> 00:10:54,280
Well, I'm also a writer with a
serial in Weekly Sapphire, so...

209
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,240
I could make the arrangements for you.

210
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:57,060
Really?

211
00:10:57,580 --> 00:11:02,400
In return,
I'll take 50% of the profits as royalties.

212
00:11:04,360 --> 00:11:12,640
That's greedy! If you don't like it, that's fine.
You're the only one who can persuade the Ai no Miko sensei and the anime staff, you know.

213
00:11:15,060 --> 00:11:21,020
What should we do? Well, we've got no choice but to say yes.
If you think of it as advertising costs, it's a necessary expense.

214
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:23,020
Understood, Ryo-san.

215
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:25,120
Thank you in advance.

216
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:28,820
Leave everything to me here.

217
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:34,900
While Minuet 7 is off in Europe,
we could make some money.

218
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:40,260
The agent for Ai no Miko?

219
00:11:40,460 --> 00:11:44,400
Yes, we'd really like to meet the
person in charge of the anime staff.

220
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:52,000
Sorry to keep you waiting.
This is the director's wife.

221
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:56,720
Actually, I'm the producer, Matsuyama.

222
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,360
I'm Yamagishi, series composition.

223
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:02,400
I'm Yamauchi, animation director.

224
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,300
I'm Shibayama, art director.

225
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:08,240
I'm Kiyokawa, director of photography.

226
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:10,240
Sound director...

227
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:15,220
Hold on, hold on! Why are there so many directors?
Who's in charge here?

228
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:19,760
W-well,
technically I'm the overall director,

229
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:22,580
then the rest of you don't get
to call yourselves directors!

230
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:25,316
In anime, the work is highly specialized,

231
00:12:25,366 --> 00:12:28,480
so each field has its own director.

232
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,376
By the way, on Minuet,

233
00:12:30,426 --> 00:12:33,160
each section has 47 people in charge.

234
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:36,858
Are you the Forty-Seven Ronin or what?
Five of you, the main ones,

235
00:12:36,908 --> 00:12:39,680
stay behind, and the rest can go home.

236
00:12:44,040 --> 00:12:44,525
Actually,

237
00:12:44,575 --> 00:12:49,040
today we came to convey a firm
request from the original author.

238
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,760
Are you saying we should
use that tambourine?

239
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:59,400
That's right. With this tambourine,
the protagonist Kisaragi Ai transforms.

240
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:01,940
Look, the transformation
pose goes like this.

241
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:05,020
Baran ri baren ra bateren ren

242
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:08,320
Kurukuru miracle lovely change!

243
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,860
Transform into what, exactly?

244
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:14,700
We've had complaints before
demanding we stick to the original,

245
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,820
but this is the first time the original
author has complained like this.

246
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:22,020
The author wants originality for the anime.

247
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:26,340
But if we bring out something like that,
the original's worldview will collapse.

248
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:32,260
Finding a way around that is where anime professionals show their skill,
isn't it?

249
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:36,660
If you can't do it,
the anime will be cancelled immediately.

250
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:40,440
That's a problem.
Production is already well underway.

251
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:45,400
Then from episode 2 onward, Kisaragi Ai
transforms with the transformation tambourine set.

252
00:13:45,400 --> 00:13:48,280
Make this a decided matter, understood?

253
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:03,520
I know this tambourine.

254
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:05,580
I think it goes like this:

255
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:11,260
Paranni paretta bateren ti

256
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:14,120
Rubukuru miracle, Lagri change!

257
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,040
W-what is this...

258
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:29,145
Love has transformed.

259
00:14:29,195 --> 00:14:31,760
Into the form of a beautiful warrior!

260
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,720
Wow, we watched it, episode 2!

261
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:44,900
Thanks to that,
wholesale orders have been pouring in.

262
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,347
Thank you very much. The promised fee,

263
00:14:47,397 --> 00:14:50,220
we've already transferred
it to Dr. Ryōchi's account.

264
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:54,940
So today I brought something like this,

265
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:57,560
Puppy and Yappy.

266
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:00,340
Could these also be made
to shine in the show?

267
00:15:01,460 --> 00:15:03,540
As for the company order,
it's the same as last time.

268
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:06,560
Leave everything to me.

269
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,180
Thank you very much.

270
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:14,100
Excuse me, I was told that
Ai-sensei's representative is here?

271
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:14,800
That would be me.

272
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,540
Are you Mr. Ryotsu?

273
00:15:16,980 --> 00:15:19,540
Nice to meet you. This is my card.

274
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:24,520
Actually, we were hoping our
products could be featured in Minuet.

275
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:26,980
So you want to become a sponsor?

276
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,300
Very well! I'll take care of everything!

277
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:35,360
You want that mascot to appear
starting from the next episode?

278
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,412
That's right! Ai Kisaragi's merry friends,

279
00:15:38,462 --> 00:15:40,120
Puppy and Yappy!

280
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:42,540
Even if it's what the original author wants,

281
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:46,360
the storyboards are already
done and animation has begun.

282
00:15:47,140 --> 00:15:52,580
It's fine. If they just add three cuts after cut 282,
we can make it work.

283
00:15:52,580 --> 00:15:56,960
But there's no delivery character who usually shows up in it,
is there?

284
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:59,620
Right, I forgot to mention that.

285
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:03,000
We're getting a new sponsor this time.

286
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,340
This one!

287
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:08,320
Ochazuke.

288
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,720
It's no good, we can't win like this.

289
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,340
Ai-chan!

290
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,380
Puppy and Yappy!

291
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,420
I brought Ai's ochazuke.

292
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:25,320
Eat this and power up!

293
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,440
Okay, got it.

294
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,120
Puppy and Yappy!

295
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:31,660
Full of vitamins, minerals, and calcium!

296
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:33,920
Eat ochazuke and power up!

297
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:36,580
When Kisaragi Ai eats Ai's ochazuke,

298
00:16:36,580 --> 00:16:39,480
she displays three times her normal power!

299
00:16:41,100 --> 00:16:41,740
Delicious!

300
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,560
Senpai, the anime's online
reactions seem kind of strange.

301
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:50,500
Ai transforms all of a sudden, and mascots
that aren't in the original keep showing up.

302
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:51,260
Just as I thought.

303
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:55,140
It seems the situation I
feared has finally happened.

304
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:56,720
The situation you feared?

305
00:16:56,920 --> 00:17:01,040
TV will use every trick to boost its ratings,
you know.

306
00:17:01,660 --> 00:17:06,200
They probably don't even think twice about
adding characters that aren't in the original.

307
00:17:07,780 --> 00:17:10,720
What am I supposed to tell
Nana-chan while she's traveling?

308
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:14,220
Is Ryotsu's agent here?

309
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:15,880
It's me, it's me.

310
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:19,020
I'll lodge a protest
about that matter on my end.

311
00:17:19,020 --> 00:17:21,820
Listen, don't say a word to Otohime Nana.

312
00:17:21,820 --> 00:17:25,020
In her case,
she might collapse from the shock.

313
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:28,340
Let's hear what you have to say here.

314
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:28,980
Yes.

315
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:31,680
No, no, a script like this won't do.

316
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:35,620
We need to make the product
play a more effective role.

317
00:17:35,620 --> 00:17:39,140
To the point where I can't
stand how badly I want a child.

318
00:17:39,140 --> 00:17:41,380
Subliminally, like, jan-jaan!

319
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:44,820
But Minuet is, after all,
a romance-type character.

320
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,240
It's impossible to include
elements other than love.

321
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:49,920
That's right.

322
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:52,000
I've thought about that point too.

323
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,900
So Makoto gets brainwashed by the enemy,

324
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:56,840
and ends up fighting Ai.

325
00:17:56,840 --> 00:17:58,760
In this giant robot, you see.

326
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,640
Editor-in-chief, I'm back.

327
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:04,440
Good work.

328
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:06,080
As for the Ai no Miko sensei,

329
00:18:06,080 --> 00:18:08,760
she plans to stay in
Europe for a while longer.

330
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:14,200
There's quite a pile of
fan letters for the Miko

331
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:16,940
This is...

332
00:18:23,860 --> 00:18:24,500
Editor-in-chief

333
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:28,480
Have you been keeping up
with the anime's fan mail?

334
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:31,140
Well, I've been busy with a lot of things.

335
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:32,400
What's wrong?

336
00:18:32,940 --> 00:18:35,000
We're getting a ton of complaints.

337
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:35,380
What?

338
00:18:36,280 --> 00:18:38,840
The white box for next week's
broadcast was sent over.

339
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:40,080
Let's check it.

340
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:43,720
But judging from what I
saw of the first episode...

341
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,900
It's strictly faithful to the principles!

342
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:48,245
Unprecedented in the world, love, evil,

343
00:18:48,295 --> 00:18:50,760
is dyeing Aokigahara red with blood!

344
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,160
W-what the heck is this!

345
00:19:04,440 --> 00:19:07,040
Kisaragi Ai! This is the finishing blow!

346
00:19:07,740 --> 00:19:11,200
Dragon Warrior-kun,
isn't this a video from a different anime?

347
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:13,560
But didn't he just clearly say
"Kisaragi Ai" and

348
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:16,900
Makoto-kun, why, why?

349
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:20,400
After all,
we were destined never to be together.

350
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,280
That line just now

351
00:19:22,280 --> 00:19:26,220
is from page 22 of volume
4 of the original comic.

352
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:29,420
So this really is the Menuet, after all?

353
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,120
Yes.

354
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:33,900
Ladies, how did you get all the way here?

355
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:36,940
With this Miyako bicycle's
Menuet and its protection,

356
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:39,060
no matter how bad the road,
it's a piece of cake.

357
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:41,580
Buppy and Yakki are here too, you know.

358
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:42,420
Ai-chan.

359
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:44,220
And Toppy too.

360
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:45,080
Ai-chan.

361
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:47,060
The one I just developed.

362
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:49,160
I brought Ai's ochazuke.

363
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:51,980
With this alone,
the power is ten times greater.

364
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:52,940
Thank you.

365
00:19:52,940 --> 00:19:54,820
Buppy, Yakki, Toppy.

366
00:19:55,260 --> 00:19:56,740
The ochazuke's flavor is the best.

367
00:19:56,740 --> 00:19:58,380
Power up with this.

368
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:00,420
Yes, it's the two-stage transformation.

369
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:01,620
Got it.

370
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:03,740
Saber type

371
00:20:03,740 --> 00:20:05,120
Two-step transformation

372
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,900
Peniet Super Arm

373
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:09,780
Spark

374
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:19,620
All five together!
Super RX Service Spark Motion!

375
00:20:20,600 --> 00:20:24,960
Our costumes are on sale now in the children's
clothing department of the department store!

376
00:20:24,960 --> 00:20:26,460
Please buy the figures too!

377
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,700
Menuet Machine

378
00:20:31,740 --> 00:20:33,180
Everyone, let's go!

379
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:34,140
OK!

380
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:36,280
Angent

381
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:38,080
Coordination!

382
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,040
Bam! Bam!

383
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:51,820
Mereddo Robo!

384
00:20:52,500 --> 00:20:54,680
Now on sale at toy stores nationwide!

385
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:58,720
Pakimoko, only 9,980 yen!

386
00:20:59,420 --> 00:21:01,720
My mecha goes on sale soon too!

387
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,020
Makoto-kun

388
00:21:06,660 --> 00:21:07,440
Even so,

389
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:10,080
even so, I still love you.

390
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,340
Forever

391
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:13,460
I'll keep waiting for you forever.

392
00:21:14,720 --> 00:21:17,140
This is no longer a minuet.

393
00:21:17,140 --> 00:21:18,120
It's an old man.

394
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,820
Cancel it immediately!

395
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:25,720
Damn the editorial department!

396
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:27,400
They went and pulled the plug on it!

397
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:29,520
What do you mean by this, Ryo-san?

398
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:32,180
We made it exactly the way you told us to.

399
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,680
What are we supposed to do now?

400
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:37,180
No anime has been decided for this time slot yet,
you know.

401
00:21:37,180 --> 00:21:38,840
Shut up, don't worry about it.

402
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:41,220
I'll prepare the next show myself.

403
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:42,960
Same as Minuet.

404
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:46,540
It's a super-popular manga
serialized in Weekly Sapphire.

405
00:21:46,540 --> 00:21:48,880
We'll start airing this next week.

406
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:51,100
Don't tell me that work is...

407
00:21:51,100 --> 00:21:53,900
Of course, it's Robo Deka Bancho!

408
00:21:59,260 --> 00:22:00,160
That's an amazing drawing.

409
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:02,440
They turned my art style
straight into animation.

410
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:05,560
Robo Deka Bancho, for the good guys!

411
00:22:07,100 --> 00:22:07,900
Whose voice is this?

412
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:12,180
Surprisingly,
I'm the one singing the theme song.

413
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:14,380
By the way, I also voice the main character.

414
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:19,000
But I never expected your
manga to become an anime, senpai.

415
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,440
What happened to Mennet?

416
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,260
It was cancelled by the
editorial department's decision.

417
00:22:23,980 --> 00:22:26,240
It's fine, it's fine.

418
00:22:26,240 --> 00:22:28,880
That's not the real Minuet.

419
00:22:29,300 --> 00:22:32,760
Even while saying that, they've gone
and bought the related merchandise.

420
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,680
Sad, the nature of fans, isn't it?

421
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:37,800
An anime with no individuality, like Minuet,

422
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:40,120
was destined to be
cancelled sooner or later.

423
00:22:40,120 --> 00:22:43,640
Well, take a look at my
distinctive Robo Deka Bancho.

424
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:45,320
Go! Robo Deka!

425
00:22:47,260 --> 00:22:49,240
Mirror! Locker!

426
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:52,220
It really is a distinctive anime.

427
00:22:54,020 --> 00:22:55,300
Right, right, isn't it?

428
00:22:55,300 --> 00:22:59,480
The centre of attention in the anime
world this year is Robo Deka Bancho!

429
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:05,040
It certainly got people talking, didn't it.

430
00:23:05,040 --> 00:23:08,220
The ratings were so low they
couldn't even be measured.

431
00:23:08,220 --> 00:23:11,900
It broke the record for the fastest cancellation,
in just one week.

432
00:23:11,900 --> 00:23:13,480
Merchandise sales: zero.

433
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:15,540
Anime history popularity poll: zero.

434
00:23:15,540 --> 00:23:17,960
It broke every record for the lowest.

435
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:20,800
Mr. Ryotsu.

436
00:23:21,920 --> 00:23:23,260
What do you want?

437
00:23:23,900 --> 00:23:24,780
What on earth do you want?

438
00:23:24,900 --> 00:23:27,014
When Robo Deka Bancho started,

439
00:23:27,064 --> 00:23:31,240
we agreed that you'd get
50% of the profits, right?

440
00:23:31,420 --> 00:23:32,920
W-well, yes, that's right.

441
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:36,886
Since Robo Deka Bancho's
merchandise took a massive loss,

442
00:23:36,936 --> 00:23:39,920
we've come to collect 50% of the deficit.

443
00:23:40,020 --> 00:23:40,880
That's ridiculous!

444
00:23:41,100 --> 00:23:44,560
That was the deal! Pay up!

445
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:47,040
Come on! Come on! Come on!

446
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:53,020
See, seriously!

447
00:23:54,080 --> 00:23:57,200
Argh! I'm so done with anime!

448
00:24:00,660 --> 00:24:02,140
Robo Deka Bancho!

449
00:24:11,260 --> 00:24:14,520
For the bad guys, the Robo Deka Punch!

450
00:24:15,940 --> 00:24:19,440
Blast them to the ends of the galaxy!

451
00:24:22,400 --> 00:24:25,860
For the cowardly ones, Robo-deka mincemeat!

452
00:24:27,140 --> 00:24:31,060
Vanish into the driftwood of the Pacific!

453
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:37,000
Ban ban ban ban ban ban chu!

454
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:40,280
Ban ban ban ban ban ban chu!

455
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:43,340
Came along with Arabi.

456
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:47,320
This is Robo Deka Bancho.

457
00:25:00,420 --> 00:25:04,580
Bancho, ban ban ban ban ban ban Bancho!

458
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:07,580
Came along with Arabi.

459
00:25:08,280 --> 00:25:09,820
This is Robo Deka.

460
00:25:10,360 --> 00:25:12,260
Buancheon!

461
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:26,300
The dream of the vast sky
that everyone held as a boy,

462
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:29,220
the friendship bonded by model airplanes.

463
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:33,720
Don't give up. Believe you will surely win,
and you will surely win.

464
00:25:34,460 --> 00:25:37,560
Next time: Wings of Friendship.
See you then!

